      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wondering if the whole getting a new drawWriter here really adds any clarity to loop or if this could all be handled internally by the drawWriter. Like as a user I\u0027m not why I\u0027m getting a new DrawWriter here. Like does it seem cleaner out here to just say:\n\nif (pipelineChange) {\n    drawWriter.newPipelineState(primitiveType, vertexStride, instanceStride):\n} else if (stateChange) {\n    drawWriter.dynamicStateChanged();\n}\n\nLike if we changed the work to \"write out\" the draws to just be a function on DrawWriter, the implementation of those functions above could just write out the draws (by calling that function) and then reset the state appropriately.\n\nI also think doing this would make the large comment in DrawWriter simpler in that you can just have a line that says: \"When state changes you must notify the DrawWriter either through newPipelineState or dynamicStateChanged\". You don\u0027t really have to show a copy of this loop in the comment then (this code is already an example of such a loop and the comment doesn\u0027t add as much).",
